Below is a practical, step‑by‑step playbook for building a modern, production‑ready frontend for an e‑commerce site.  
I’ll cover the whole pipeline—from design to deployment—so you can pick the parts that fit your team’s skill set and project scope.

---

## 1️⃣ Define the Scope & Gather Requirements

| Item | Why it matters | Typical outcome |
|------|----------------|-----------------|
| **Target audience** | Determines design language, accessibility needs, and device mix. | Personas, user journeys |
| **Core features** | Shopping cart, product catalog, search, filters, checkout, user account, reviews, admin panel. | Feature list, priority matrix |
| **Performance goals** | Page load time, time‑to‑interactive, SEO score. | Target metrics (e.g., < 2 s on mobile) |
| **Compliance** | GDPR, PCI‑DSS, WCAG 2.1. | Legal checklist |
| **Budget & timeline** | Influences tech stack, third‑party services, and hiring. | Project plan |

> **Tip:** Create a *Product Requirements Document* (PRD) that captures all of the above. It becomes the single source of truth for designers, developers, and stakeholders.

---

## 2️⃣ Design Phase

| Tool | Use case | Why it’s useful |
|------|----------|-----------------|
| **Figma / Sketch / Adobe XD** | Wireframes → High‑fidelity mockups → Interactive prototypes | Collaboration, version control, component libraries |
| **Storybook** | UI component library documentation | Reusable components, visual regression testing |
| **Zeplin / Avocode** | Handoff to dev | Auto‑generated CSS, assets, specs |
| **Accessibility audit** (axe, Lighthouse) | Ensure WCAG compliance | Better UX, SEO, legal safety |

### Design Checklist

1. **Responsive grid** – mobile‑first, then tablet, desktop.  
2. **Color palette & typography** – consistent brand identity.  
3. **Component hierarchy** – product card, filter panel, cart drawer, modal, etc.  
4. **Interaction patterns** – hover states, focus rings, ARIA roles.  
5. **Micro‑interactions** – add‑to‑cart animation, toast notifications.  

---

## 3️⃣ Choose the Tech Stack

| Category | Options | Pros | Cons |
|----------|---------|------|------|
| **Framework** | React, Vue, Angular, Svelte | Mature ecosystems, component‑based | Learning curve, bundle size |
| **State management** | Redux / Zustand / Pinia / NgRx | Predictable state, devtools | Boilerplate |
| **Styling** | CSS Modules / Tailwind / Styled‑Components | Scoped styles, utility‑first | CSS‑in‑JS overhead |
| **Routing** | React Router / Vue Router / Angular Router | Declarative routes | Requires SPA setup |
| **Build tool** | Vite / Webpack / Rollup | Fast dev server, tree‑shaking | Configuration complexity |
| **Testing** | Jest + React Testing Library / Cypress | Unit + E2E coverage | Test maintenance |
| **CI/CD** | GitHub Actions / GitLab CI / CircleCI | Automation, reproducibility | Requires pipeline setup |

> **Recommendation for most e‑commerce sites:**  
> **React + Vite + Tailwind + Zustand** – fast, lightweight, and highly composable.

---

## 4️⃣ Architecture Overview

```
┌───────────────────────┐
│  UI Layer (React)     │
│  ├─ Components         │
│  ├─ Pages              │
│  └─ Hooks              │
├───────────────────────┤
│  State Layer           │
│  ├─ Global Store       │
│  └─ Local State        │
├───────────────────────┤
│  Service Layer         │
│  ├─ API Clients        │
│  ├─ Auth Service       │
│  └─ Payment Service    │
├───────────────────────┤
│  Utility Layer         │
│  ├─ Validation         │
│  ├─ Formatters         │
│  └─ Error Handling     │
└───────────────────────┘
```

### Key Patterns

| Pattern | What it solves | Implementation hint |
|---------|----------------|----------------------|
| **Feature‑flagged components** | Roll out new UI gradually | `react-feature-flag` |
| **Lazy loading** | Reduce initial bundle | `React.lazy` + `Suspense` |
| **SSR / SSG** | SEO, faster first paint | Next.js, Nuxt.js, Astro |
| **Service Workers** | Offline support, caching | Workbox |
| **GraphQL** | Flexible data fetching | Apollo Client |
| **REST** | Simpler integration | Axios / Fetch |

---

## 5️⃣ Core Feature Implementation

### 5.1 Product Catalog

```tsx
// src/components/ProductCard.tsx
import { Link } from 'react-router-dom';
import { useImage } from '../hooks/useImage';

export const ProductCard = ({ product }) => {
  const { src, loading } = useImage(product.imageUrl);

  return (
    <Link to={`/product/${product.id}`} className="block">
      <div className="relative h-48 w-full overflow-hidden rounded-lg">
        {loading && <div className="absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center">Loading…</div>}
        <img src={src} alt={product.title} className="object-cover h-full w-full" />
      </div>
      <h3 className="mt-2 text-sm font-medium">{product.title}</h3>
      <p className="text-sm text-gray-600">${product.price}</p>
    </Link>
  );
};
```

- **Lazy image loading** (`useImage` hook)  
- **Skeleton placeholders** for better UX  
- **SSR** for SEO (Next.js page)

### 5.2 Search & Filters

```tsx
// src/pages/ShopPage.tsx
import { useSearchParams } from 'react-router-dom';
import { useProducts } from '../hooks/useProducts';

export const ShopPage = () => {
  const [searchParams] = useSearchParams();
  const { products, loading } = useProducts(searchParams);

  return (
    <div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
      <aside className="md:col-span-1">
        {/* Filter components */}
      </aside>
      <main className="md:col-span-3">
        {loading ? <Spinner /> : <ProductGrid products={products} />}
      </main>
    </div>
  );
};
```

- **Query‑string driven filters** → bookmarkable URLs  
- **Debounced search** to reduce API calls  
- **Server‑side filtering** for large catalogs

### 5.3 Shopping Cart

```tsx
// src/store/cartSlice.ts
import { createSlice } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';

const cartSlice = createSlice({
  name: 'cart',
  initialState: { items: [], total: 0 },
  reducers: {
    addItem: (state, action) => {
      const item = action.payload;
      const existing = state.items.find(i => i.id === item.id);
      if (existing) existing.quantity += item.quantity;
      else state.items.push(item);
      state.total += item.price * item.quantity;
    },
    removeItem: (state, action) => {
      const id = action.payload;
      const item = state.items.find(i => i.id === id);
      if (item) {
        state.total -= item.price * item.quantity;
        state.items = state.items.filter(i => i.id !== id);
      }
    },
    clearCart: state => {
      state.items = [];
      state.total = 0;
    },
  },
});

export const { addItem, removeItem, clearCart } = cartSlice.actions;
export default cartSlice.reducer;
```

- **Persist cart** in `localStorage` or `IndexedDB`  
- **Optimistic UI** for add/remove actions  
- **Sync with backend** on checkout

### 5.4 Checkout Flow

1. **Address form** – auto‑complete, validation  
2. **Payment integration** – Stripe Elements, PayPal SDK  
3. **Order confirmation** – email webhook, order status page  
4. **Error handling** – retry logic, fallback UI

```tsx
// src/components/CheckoutForm.tsx
